# Vendored, byte for byte.
#
# `libheif.js` is a minified Emscripten build copied verbatim from
# libheif-js@1.19.8 and README.md records its sha384. On a Windows checkout
# git's line-ending conversion would rewrite every LF in it, which changes that
# hash and makes "is this still the file we vendored?" unanswerable. The .wasm
# is already treated as binary by content detection; this says so out loud for
# both, so neither depends on a guess.
*.js -text
*.wasm -text binary
